/-!
# The absolute Galois group of a finite field

Source: literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors-basics/sk-lem-base-field-cd/
sk-lem-base-field-cd-galois-group.md (blueprint: det-base-field-cd-galois-group).

## Main statements

* For a finite field, the unique degree-`n` intermediate field in a separable closure is
  the root field of `X^(q^n) - X` and its automorphism group is generated by Frobenius.
* The absolute Galois group is the profinite completion of the infinite cyclic group,
  with arithmetic Frobenius corresponding to its canonical generator.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

open scoped Polynomial

/-- The finite-field absolute Galois group statement, including its finite cyclic quotients.

Source: literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors-basics/
sk-lem-base-field-cd/sk-lem-base-field-cd-galois-group.md, paragraphs 1--2
(blueprint: det-base-field-cd-galois-group).

Proof plan:
1. Write `q = p ^ a` with `a ≥ 1` using `def-weil-finite-field-q-elements`, hence `q ≥ 2`.
   By `lem-sfb-finite-field-separable-closure-algebraic`, the given separable closure is an
   algebraic closure. Apply `lem-weil-unique-subfield-of-closure` to construct the roots
   of `X ^ (q ^ n) - X`, containing `K`, with cardinality `q ^ n` and unique of that cardinality.
2. A basis-coordinate bijection gives `|V| = q ^ dim V`. The finite root field is
   finite-dimensional by `def-weil-finite-dimensional-subspace`; comparing powers of `q ≥ 2`
   gives degree `n`. Conversely every degree-`n` intermediate field has `q ^ n` elements,
   so the cardinality uniqueness in step 1 proves uniqueness among all degree-`n` fields.
3. Apply `lem-sfb-finite-field-galois-frobenius`: the extension is Galois, Frobenius has
   order `n`, and its first `n` powers are all automorphisms. Thus `[j] ↦ φn ^ j` identifies
   the additive group `ZMod n` with this Galois group, sending `1` to Frobenius.
4. By `def-weil-frobenius-substitution`, arithmetic Frobenius on the closure is `x ↦ x ^ q`.
   It preserves each root field and restricts to its Frobenius. If `d ∣ n`, iteration of
   `x ^ (q ^ d) = x` gives inclusion of root fields. Conversely inclusion forces the
   degree-`d` Frobenius to have `n`-th power one; division with remainder and its order `d`
   give `d ∣ n`. Every finite subextension is one of these fields by degree uniqueness;
   `def-pd-separable-closure` puts every element in such a finite subextension.
5. By `lem-weil-pbc-separable-closure-exists-galois`, the closure extension is Galois.
   Apply `lem-exc-galois-krull-finite-limit` (Stacks Tag 0BU2): restriction identifies its
   Galois group with the profinite limit over all finite Galois intermediate fields.
   Step 4 identifies that indexing poset with positive integers ordered by divisibility.
6. Restriction sends `φn ^ j` to `φd ^ j`, so the cyclic identifications of step 3 identify
   the transition maps with reduction of residues. Coordinate maps and inverses are
   continuous (finite groups are discrete), hence give a homeomorphism of the product
   subspaces of compatible tuples. These tuples are the profinite completion of additive
   `ℤ`, expressed here using `Multiplicative ℤ`; its finite-index subgroups are `nℤ` for
   positive `n`. Frobenius maps to `(1 mod n)` at every coordinate, the image under `etaFn`
   of `Multiplicative.ofAdd (1 : ℤ)`.
-/
theorem finiteField_absoluteGaloisGroup
    (K : Type u) (Ks : Type v) [Field K] [Field Ks] [Fintype K] [Algebra K Ks]
    [IsSepClosure K Ks] :
    ∃ φ : Gal(Ks / K),
      (∀ x : Ks, φ x = x ^ Fintype.card K) ∧
      (∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n →
        ∃ Kn : IntermediateField K Ks,
          Module.finrank K Kn = n ∧
          (∀ E : IntermediateField K Ks, Module.finrank K E = n → E = Kn) ∧
          (∀ x : Ks,
            x ∈ Kn ↔
              Polynomial.eval₂ (algebraMap K Ks) x
                (Polynomial.X ^ (Fintype.card K ^ n) - Polynomial.X) = 0) ∧
          IsGalois K Kn ∧
          ∃ φn : Kn ≃ₐ[K] Kn,
            (∀ x : Kn, φn x = x ^ Fintype.card K) ∧
            orderOf φn = n ∧
            (∀ g : Kn ≃ₐ[K] Kn, ∃ j : ZMod n, g = φn ^ j.val)) ∧
      ∃ e : Gal(Ks / K) ≃ₜ* ProfiniteGrp.ProfiniteCompletion.completion
          (GrpCat.of (Multiplicative ℤ)),
        e φ =
          ProfiniteGrp.ProfiniteCompletion.etaFn (GrpCat.of (Multiplicative ℤ))
            (Multiplicative.ofAdd (1 : ℤ)) := by
  sorry

end
